<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/pages/seperate/seperate.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/pages/seperate/seperatemodal.css">
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <h1>Seperation of frontend and backend</h1>

        <ul>
                    <h3><a href="/">Back to index</a></h3>
                    <h3>Reasons to seperate</h3>
                        <p>What should you be able to see as a end user</p>
                        <p>Build a folder for the public use and folders backend infrastructure</p>
                        <p class="clickable" id="renderQuestion">How do you render?</p>

                     <!-- Modal -->
                 <div id="renderModal" class="modal">
                <div class="modal-content">
                 <span class="close">&times;</span>
                   <h3>How rendering works</h3>
                     <p>Rendering is sending data from the backend to the frontend.</p>
                    <p>If you don't render the data is never shown on the frontend.</p>
                    <p>You should make seperate connections for each use. Use DTOs if possible</p>
                 </div>
             </div>


        </ul>
    </main>

<script src="/pages/seperate/modal.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
